2026-09-27T09:10:26.5660079Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5660362Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5660787Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5661217Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5661359Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5661682Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5661873Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5662097Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5662777Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5663750Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5663984Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5664430Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5664701Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5664920Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5665495Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5666029Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5667156Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5668051Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5668226Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5668951Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5669852Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5670329Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5671225Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5671940Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5672083Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5672393Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5754961Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5757163Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5759469Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5759831Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5760556Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5761742Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5762659Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5763725Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5764390Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5765030Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5765188Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5765762Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5766019Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5767668Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5769451Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5770459Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5771789Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:26.5772110Z 
